// `system.uptime()` reads the telemetry receiver the checker resolves by name.
// No corpus file declares `system`, so the pass loaded the name, reported E2001
// for the load and E2005 for the call that used it. `compiler/front/sema.orb`
// answers `system` for the identifier and `int` for each of its ten methods, so
// this pass reads that answer: the receiver is `load system system` and the call
// carries `int`. A local named `system` is read before the builtin, the way the
// checker reads it.
import "../../compiler/tir/entry.orb"

fn main() {
    val source = "fn up() -> int { return system.uptime() }"
    print(compileFrontendSource("fixture", source))
}
